From 2aba3279faf6354b34206e16d0b1d3c94a77d64d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:26:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 296/297] PM: console: do not force a VT switch when console
 suspend is disabled

With no_console_suspend, pm_vt_switch() always switched to the suspend
console, so on resume the phone's panel showed the text console instead
of the compositor's screen until the next key press. The kernel messages
still reach every console (pstore's included) without the switch, so only
drivers that ask for one get it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel/power/console.c | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/power/console.c b/kernel/power/console.c
index 33ace63b1088..f293fc5c4383 100644
--- a/kernel/power/console.c
+++ b/kernel/power/console.c
@@ -97,12 +97,15 @@ void pm_vt_switch_unregister(struct device *dev)
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(pm_vt_switch_unregister);
 
 /*
- * There are three cases when a VT switch on suspend/resume are required:
+ * There are two cases when a VT switch on suspend/resume is required:
  *   1) no driver has indicated a requirement one way or another, so preserve
  *      the old behavior
- *   2) console suspend is disabled, we want to see debug messages across
- *      suspend/resume
- *   3) any registered driver indicates it needs a VT switch
+ *   2) any registered driver indicates it needs a VT switch
+ *
+ * Console suspend being disabled (no_console_suspend) no longer forces one:
+ * the messages still reach every console, pstore's included, and on a phone
+ * the switch left the text console on the panel at resume instead of the
+ * compositor's (switched-off) screen.
  *
  * If none of these conditions is present, meaning we have at least one driver
  * that doesn't need the switch, and none that do, we can avoid it to make
@@ -118,9 +121,6 @@ static bool pm_vt_switch(void)
 	if (list_empty(&pm_vt_switch_list))
 		goto out;
 
-	if (!console_suspend_enabled)
-		goto out;
-
 	list_for_each_entry(entry, &pm_vt_switch_list, head) {
 		if (entry->required)
 			goto out;
